                          "change": "run.py: added a cached 0-dim -0.125 constant tensor; _affine(x,y) computes out = torch.add(offset, y, alpha=0.75); out.add_(x, alpha=1.25); out.relu_() — three kernels, one allocation, inputs never mutated. run() first checks a bounded CUDA-graph cache matched by tensor identity + _version (holding strong refs to x and y so pointers cannot be recycled), replays and returns the graph's static output on hit. On a second consecutive call with identical input objects, _maybe_capture() warms up on a side stream and captures the three kernels; any exception disables capture permanently and the eager path is used. Non-equal shapes fall back to the literal reference expression to preserve broadcast semantics. get_inputs/get_test_cases/get_benchmark_inputs/reference untouched.",
