                      "title": "Remove redundant clone() and intermediate temporaries in run(inputs)",
                      "direction": "run(inputs) now allocates `out = torch.empty_like(x)` once and performs: torch.mul(x, 1.25, out=out); torch.add(out, y, alpha=0.75, out=out); torch.sub(out, 0.125, out=out); out.relu_(); return out. No clone, no intermediate tensors, no full-tensor temporaries. Inputs are never mutated (x is only read, y is only read), so repeated calls and the independent reference oracle are unaffected. Numerically identical to reference: same FP32 op order per element (x*1.25, + y*0.75, - 0.125, relu), well inside atol=rtol=1e-5.",
